{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of PostHog’s batch capture API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder.swift#L76","fileName":"PostHogBatchEncoder.swift"},"title":"PostHogBatchEncoder","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:15PostHogEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and PostHog’s limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"text":" with two members: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"api_key"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project token, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: "},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and "},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracked by a tracker without "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which keeps no context) is its own anonymous person, linked to nothing: PostHog rejects a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch when one of its events has no "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". PostHog counts a person per "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so its unique users are sessions. The session is also sent as "},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which PostHog’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions and web analytics group events by ("},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context value, aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":". A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property whose name starts with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":", which only a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":" conformance can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write, or is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":", is left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names as settings (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$set"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile"},{"text":") or the identity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mobile"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tablet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Desktop"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TV"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vision"},{"type":"text","text":" for the form factor; no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"},{"type":"text","text":" for a watch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$locale"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$network_wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$network_cellular"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_version","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value JSON can’t, and one too large for PostHog to store ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. PostHog answers a batch it takes with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it rejects. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"t